  "main_text": "<think>\nOkay, let's start by understanding what the user needs. Lucas Brown wants to return items from different orders and make some changes to a pending order. First, I need to authenticate his identity. He provided his email, so I'll use find_user_id_by_email.\n\nOnce authenticated, I'll check each request. He wants to return bookshelves and jigsaw puzzles from different orders. For each, I need to get the order details to confirm they're delivered. Then, use return_delivered_order_items for each order. \n\nNext, he wants to return a backpack with the vacuum cleaner. That's another order, so same process. \n\nFor the pending order, he wants to change the item to red and update the address. I'll check the order status, then modify the items and address. Need to confirm all details and get his approval before each action. \n\nAlso, he wants the tracking number of a cancelled order. I'll retrieve that once the cancellation is confirmed. \n\nEach step requires a tool call and user confirmation. I'll handle one at a time as per policy.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"find_user_id_by_email\", \"arguments\": {\"email\": \"lucas.brown9344@example.com\"}}\n",
